|---|---|
| Frames after warmup | 1801 |
| FPS | **60** (`targetFrameRate` cap) |
| Frame p50 / p95 / p99 | 16.67 / **16.72** / 16.83 ms |
| Physics2D | **0.17 ms** |
| FixedUpdate scripts | **0.13 ms** |
| Render marker | 0 (batch did not catch URP) |
| `maxFixedSteps` | 4, once **5** (frame 26.7 ms around t=9) |
| GC.Alloc | ~34 bytes/frame |

`Main Thread` ≈ 16.66 ms here equals the 60 FPS frame length: the
`WaitForTargetFPS` marker in batch is almost zero, so `busyMain` cannot
be taken from it. Physics+scripts work ≈ **0.3 ms**. There is no step
spiral.

**Verdict:** the main thread is in the green zone. Do not cut 200 Hz.
Next is swing liftoff on walk, not a new profile and not 100 Hz.

